{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1403839-fighting-spirits-and-the-lex-magica","id":1403839,"title":"Fighting spirits and the Lex Magica","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-21T10:52:04-07:00","id":1403839,"title":"Fighting spirits and the Lex Magica","content":"In the book Signs of Sorcery (which is a great book by the way), it says that the Exarchs have legions of spirits at their command. It then later on goes on that the policy of most mages is to flee or try to subdue the spirit without harming it because, well, harming spirits goes against the Lex Magica. Sure some Adamantine Arrow's might argue that it is in self defence, but, looking at the rules, it seems that harming a spirit or binding it against it's will is an act of Hubris which most Mages try to avoid.<br /> <br /> How would Mages approach this. I am sure that they are assailed by Exarch loyal spirits all the time, but this indicates that they cannot fight back and have got one hand tied behind their back. What would a diamond mage do in such a case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T11:04:40-07:00","id":1403844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1403839-fighting-spirits-and-the-lex-magica#post1403839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the book Signs of Sorcery (which is a great book by the way), it says that the Exarchs have legions of spirits at their command. It then later on goes on that the policy of most mages is to flee or try to subdue the spirit without harming it because, well, harming spirits goes against the Lex Magica. Sure some Adamantine Arrow's might argue that it is in self defence, but, looking at the rules, it seems that harming a spirit or binding it against it's will is an act of Hubris which most Mages try to avoid.<br /> <br /> How would Mages approach this. I am sure that they are assailed by Exarch loyal spirits all the time, but this indicates that they cannot fight back and have got one hand tied behind their back. What would a diamond mage do in such a case?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not spirits, it's Supernal entities. I'm sure they'd have no qualms wiping out spirits.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery, p122: 'As tyrants of the Supernal, the Exarchs command legions; choirs of recording gods and lesser Exarchs spoken of in Seer mythology and assumed to reside in the deep Supernal Realm, but also the lesser, more understandable Supernal entities mages encounter in the Supernal World of Mage Sight or summon forth for boons.'<br /> <br /> 'The Lex Magica still regards the destruction of a Supernal Entity as a crime even if that entity is hostile, and almost all Consilia advise mages to retreat in the face of Supernal aggression, or to neutralize the entity without destroying it. The exceptions include Consilia that have come under protracted attack by Seer-summoned entities; the Budapest Incident of 1997, for example, led to that Consilium\u2019s members having their right to self-defense enshrined.'<br /> <br /> That said, using a ban or bane to keep them away from your sanctum or yourself, probably doesn't count as an act of Hubris, especially if you're not whipping it up with a spell. Supernal entities tend to be weirdly fragile though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-21-2020, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T11:10:35-07:00","id":1403845,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...very interesting. I thought that a Spirit was a sort of Supernal Entity but I could be mistaken.<br /> <br /> That does make the whole situation require some thinking. I know that Seers of the Throne, with 4 dots of Prelacy, can basically make a Demise which will be crawling with Exarchial Entities, probably a good hedge against the local Consilium. Alternatively, Seers can summon Entities to them and direct them to the local diamond mages and see how they deal with it. This seems like a major challenge for diamond mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T11:29:33-07:00","id":1403850,"title":"","content":"Yeah - it's Supernal Entities the Pentacle have problems with killing, due to most of them believing it causes damage to the universe when you do so. That the Seers have a slightly easier time with Supernal Entities by dint of the Exarchs ruling the Supernal Realm is just... tough. Something the Pentacle has to bear in mind, and another reason why the cold war between the Sects remains mostly cold - assaulting a Seer sanctum with a Temple in it is <i>serious business</i>.<br /> <br /> Spirits from the Shadow Realm, the Pentacle has no problem abusing as long as it doesn't cause another mage problems. Don't fuck with the resonance influencing your neighbours' ley lines, don't let hordes across the Gauntlet for no good reason, and you can buy off as many spirit courts and make as many hybridised monstrosities as you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T11:43:39-07:00","id":1403853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1403839-fighting-spirits-and-the-lex-magica?p=1403845#post1403845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm...very interesting. I thought that a Spirit was a sort of Supernal Entity but I could be mistaken.<br /> <br /> That does make the whole situation require some thinking. I know that Seers of the Throne, with 4 dots of Prelacy, can basically make a Demise which will be crawling with Exarchial Entities, probably a good hedge against the local Consilium. Alternatively, Seers can summon Entities to them and direct them to the local diamond mages and see how they deal with it. This seems like a major challenge for diamond mages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on how they go about it. If they send a type of ephemeral entity they can't detect under a familiar pact, they can vaporize the soul stone lynchpin from remote viewing. Space makes this even easier.<br /> <br /> Fly invisibly over an area and use Prime or Death to destroy or suppress the soul stone and they lose access to its benefits.<br /> <br /> If you are more devious, you can use a Patterning to make the Demesne into an Anullity, which neutralizes the Prelacy and can cause a crippling disruption to them in one go.<br /> <br /> There is always the option of the classic Golem or Sleeper strike team (police, thugs, etc), which has been given the benefits of <i>Wards &amp; Signs</i><br /> <br /> Lastly, you can always use a Veiling of Fate to hide / create misinformation on what the intent of &quot;serving or betraying the Exarchs&quot; means. If the Supernal Entities feel the Prelate is betraying their liege, they may take it upon themselves to...terminate the employment.<br /> <br /> There are lots of ways to go about it. But one thing is certain, you should never try to confront a Prelate in their Exarch's field of expertise, it will probably end horribly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-21-2020, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T13:23:44-07:00","id":1404079,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Seers are that keen to send a Supernal Being to fight in their stead, though. A loyal servant of the Exarchs is simply worth more than a pylon of chronic backstabbers. Mages who allow a literal messenger of the gods to die in unnecessary combat are as much in trouble as the blasphemous member of the Pentacle who killed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13425-gantolandon","name":"Gantolandon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T14:38:49-07:00","id":1404091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gantolandon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1403839-fighting-spirits-and-the-lex-magica?p=1404079#post1404079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Seers are that keen to send a Supernal Being to fight in their stead, though. A loyal servant of the Exarchs is simply worth more than a pylon of chronic backstabbers. Mages who allow a literal messenger of the gods to die in unnecessary combat are as much in trouble as the blasphemous member of the Pentacle who killed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wouldn't expect it to be a common happenstance, knowing the other Orders might balk or simply retreat in the face of it can make it an incredibly effective demonstration. You wouldn't even need to send it to actually fight, conceivably. Definitely the type of big gun you'd hold onto for when you need to tackle an Athenaeum or retrieve some unique profane urim. Like presumably the 'Budapest Incident of 1997' had some pretty hefty reason for an entire consilium to be under 'protracted attack' by Supernal entities beyond usual Seer antagonism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T15:16:52-07:00","id":1404104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gantolandon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1403839-fighting-spirits-and-the-lex-magica?p=1404079#post1404079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Seers are that keen to send a Supernal Being to fight in their stead, though. A loyal servant of the Exarchs is simply worth more than a pylon of chronic backstabbers. Mages who allow a literal messenger of the gods to die in unnecessary combat are as much in trouble as the blasphemous member of the Pentacle who killed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, you would want to have it destroyed if:<br /> <br /> 1- It tries to take control of the Pylon, sending them into dangerous or counterproductive missions.<br /> <br /> 2- Its death can be used a bargaining chip not to heat the cold war with the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> 3- It belongs to a rival Pylon, even if of the same Exarch, letting you put their &quot;gross incompetence&quot; on display.<br /> <br /> 4- It acts as a guardian to some forbidden treasure you need. So you hand the Pentacle this small victory while you walk away with the real prize.<br /> <br /> 5- It can be convinced to wield its might against your boss or rival. Whether it kills it, they take each other out or it weakens them, you are still the victor.<br /> <br /> 6- Its defeat results in the weakening or annulment of a rival Ministry's grip on the city, such as a losing the Pandemonic entity that creates a mansion connected to every shadow in the city.<br /> <br /> 7- You made a bargain with it, which you do not intend to keep. You have it eliminated to keep all the benefits.<br /> <br /> <br /> All of this is subject to what your Exarch lets you get away with and how often you push your luck compared to how adept you are at pushing its agenda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}